## Upstream work

This project implements a client for, and a port of parts of,
[Locus](https://github.com/r1n7aro/Locus) — an open-source Unity development
agent by [@r1n7aro](https://github.com/r1n7aro), also released under
GPL-3.0-or-later. It is aligned with Locus commit
[`4ee37ed0`](https://github.com/r1n7aro/Locus/tree/4ee37ed0) (v0.9.3).

Nothing here is an official Locus release, and the Locus authors are not
affiliated with this project.

## Files derived from Locus

### `native/locus_unix_native/` — Linux/macOS broker port

Derived from `crates/locus-native-broker` and `locus_unity_native/` in the
upstream repository. **Modified** for POSIX hosts:

- the Win32 named-pipe transport is replaced by a Unix domain socket server
  (`src/server.rs`, `src/names_unix.rs`);
- the named shared-memory state plane becomes a file-backed `mmap`
  (`src/state_plane.rs`);
- Mono symbol resolution uses `dlopen`/`dlsym` instead of
  `GetModuleHandle`/`GetProcAddress` (`src/mono_names.rs`);
- WebView2, GPU render transport and the in-process background hook have no
  Unix counterpart and return the platform's "unavailable" values (`src/lib.rs`).

The C ABI exported by the library is unchanged, so the unmodified upstream
managed plugin binds it on Linux as it does on Windows.

### `native/locus-native-protocol/` — wire protocol crate

Copied **unmodified** from `crates/locus-native-protocol` upstream. It defines
the newline-delimited JSON envelope, the state-plane byte layout, kernel object
naming, capability identifiers and broker error codes that both sides must agree
on. It is vendored here only so the port builds without an upstream checkout;
the path dependency in `native/locus_unix_native/Cargo.toml` was rewritten to
point at it.

If you intend to modify these files, prefer sending changes upstream so the two
implementations do not drift.

## Original work in this repository

Everything else — the DSH plugin (`src/`), its tests, scripts and documentation —
is original to this project and carries the same GPL-3.0-or-later license.

`src/pipe-name.js` is a deliberate line-by-line reimplementation of the naming
scheme in `crates/locus-native-protocol/src/names.rs`; it must stay
byte-compatible with it so both sides derive the same endpoint.
